{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Removed the no-op caller-selected reviewer input from the three public review-code entry points: the CLI parser/handler no longer accepts or forwards --reviewer, the MCP review_code tool no longer advertises a reviewers parameter, and rebar.llm.review_code() now rejects reviewers= at the Python signature. Kept the output review_result reviewers field, regenerated the CLI/MCP reference artifacts and MCP/library parity manifest, corrected ADR 0075 and changelog wording, and added focused guards for parser rejection, no-forwarding, signature rejection, and reviewers-output preservation. Focused review-code tests, lint, typecheck, cli-help/reference checks, api-surface, and MCP/library parity are green. The default broad selector still carries a pre-existing atomic-close lifecycle baseline: the already-approved test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head plus four sibling failures in the same file that reproduce unchanged on a clean origin/main snapshot."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788441206683174001,"uuid":"b92d79f2-b666-4b03-b8b8-974da9d17acc"}